{"at_ms":17682,"id":1791787443879148,"type":"voice.tool_result","payload":{"clarify":false,"detail":"The provider was refusing the extra calls, which is its way of saying slow down. The quick fix just waits a minute and tries each invoice again. The proper fix sends invoices in big batches instead of one at a time, so it cannot fall behind again.","dur_ms":10818,"id":"call_123623","name":"to_supervisor","options":["Re-run now with the quick fix","Do the proper batch fix"],"scheduling":"interrupt","scheduling_sent":"interrupt","spoken":"api-claude has finished looking into the invoice job. The job sent the invoices one at a time, but the payment provider only accepts a hundred calls a minute, and last night there were over four thousand invoices. So most of them never went out, and customers would get them a day late unless the job runs again before nine this morning. It says running it again now is safe, and would take about forty minutes. Shall I have it re-run the job now with the quick fix, or go straight to the proper one?","wait_ms":1}}
